WEBVTT

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:17.480
<v Ira Glass>Bob Harris has won two cars and a lot of money playing Jeopardy on television. But he insists he's not that smart. What he is, he says, is somebody who decided when he was going to be on Jeopardy to take measures.
<v Ira Glass>鲍勃·哈里斯在电视游戏节目《危险边缘》中赢过两辆车和一大笔奖金。但他坚持认为自己并不聪明。他说，他只是一个在决定参加《危险边缘》时就采取了相应措施的人。

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:39.940
<v Bob Harris>I told my girlfriend at the time, hi. I'm rearranging the furniture now. And I need to make my house look like the Jeopardy studio. I set up low bookcases to be sort of like where the podiums were, about the same height. And I would stand there. I had a little homemade buzzer that I made out of a ballpoint pen and some masking tape.
<v Bob Harris>我当时告诉女朋友，嘿，我现在要重新布置家具。我得让我的房子看起来像《危险边缘》的演播室。我摆放了一些矮书架，高度和讲台差不多。我会站在那里。我有一个用圆珠笔和美纹纸胶带自制的小蜂鸣器。

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:50.680
<v Ira Glass>He got bright halogen lights. And he pumped up the air conditioning to make it feel like the inside of a TV studio. He placed a big picture of Jeopardy's host, Alex Trebek, in about the spot where the real Alex Trebek stands.
<v Ira Glass>他买来了明亮的卤素灯，还调大了空调，让房间里感觉就像电视演播室内部一样。他在真正的亚历克斯·特雷贝克站立的位置附近，放了一张巨大的《危险边缘》主持人亚历克斯·特雷贝克的照片。

00:00:50.680 --> 00:01:08.160
<v Bob Harris>I even tried to time my meals to when I would be eating at Jeopardy, so that my whole body clock would be exactly in harmony.
<v Bob Harris>我甚至尝试调整我的用餐时间，以配合我在《危险边缘》中比赛的时间，这样我的生物钟就能完全合拍。

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:26.190
<v Ira Glass>So he played along with videotapes of the TV show. And he studied for months, memorizing all kinds of stuff, the guys who ran the United Nations in order, the presidents in order, rivers, the elements, British kings, the novels of E. M. Forster-- which include, by the way, Room With a View, Where Angels Fear to Tread, Howards End.
<v Ira Glass>于是他跟着电视节目的录像带一起玩。他学习了几个月，背诵了各种东西：联合国历任负责人、历任总统、河流、元素、英国国王、E.M.福斯特的小说——顺便说一下，包括《看得见风景的房间》、《天使不敢涉足的地方》、《霍华德庄园》。

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:49.840
<v Bob Harris>The way to remember a lot of stuff is to build really big, goofy images. It takes an extra couple of seconds, maybe even a minute or two of thought, but then it stays better. So it's time well invested. I made this big picture in my head of a room with a view. OK, so you've got this nice, really big, like-- a friend of mine in Ohio grew up in this big mansion, so it's actually his living room in my head. So OK, it's a room with a beautiful view.
<v Bob Harris>记住大量东西的方法是构建非常宏大、古怪的图像。这需要多花几秒钟，甚至一两分钟的时间来思考，但这样记的效果更好。所以这是值得的投资。我在脑海里画了一幅大大的“看得见风景的房间”的图。好吧，你拥有这个漂亮、特别大的房间——我在俄亥俄州的一个朋友就是在这样的豪宅里长大的，所以我脑海里用的就是他的客厅。所以，好吧，这是一个拥有美丽风景的房间。

00:01:49.840 --> 00:02:11.860
<v Bob Harris>And Howards End was the next one on the list that I just happened to have in front of me. And so Howards End , and you've got A Room With a View . I mean, how can you not have, like, Howard-- I have a friend named Howard. And so I made a 30-foot buttocks and stuck it in the window. So you have a room with a view of Howard's end where angels fear to tread. So the angels are in this room, and there's this giant 30-foot buttocks in the window.
<v Bob Harris>《霍华德庄园》是我清单上的下一部，正好就在我面前。所以《霍华德庄园》，再加上《看得见风景的房间》。我的意思是，怎么能没有“霍华德”呢——我有个朋友叫霍华德。所以我做了一个30英尺高的屁股，把它插在窗户里。这样你就拥有了一个能看到“霍华德庄园”的、天使不敢涉足的风景房间。天使就在这个房间里，窗户里还有一个30英尺高的巨大屁股。

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.790
<v Ira Glass>That's why the angels fear to tread there.
<v Ira Glass>这就是为什么天使不敢涉足那里的原因。

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:16.250
<v Bob Harris>Who really wants to be there, really?
<v Bob Harris>谁真的想待在那儿呢？

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:43.840
<v Ira Glass>All I can say is, you do not want to know how he got Passage to India in there. Bob says that a third of the answers that he gave on television-- a third-- came from cramming information into his head with these weird pictures that he would create for himself. And one of his biggest wins came when-- thanks to brute memorization-- he knew the name of an old book called The Compleat Angler, which to this day he has never read, has only the vaguest idea what it's about. And one of his biggest losses came when he could not remember the poem, "Jabberwocky."
<v Ira Glass>我只能说，你肯定不想知道他是怎么把《印度之行》塞进去的。鲍勃说，他在电视上给出的答案中，有三分之一——三分之一——来自于他用这些为自己创造的古怪图片强行塞进脑子里的信息。他最大的一次胜利是因为——多亏了死记硬背——他知道一本叫《捕鱼全书》的旧书的名字，直到今天他都没读过，甚至对它的内容只有最模糊的概念。而他最大的一次失败是因为他记不起那首《杰伯沃基》诗了。

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:56.870
<v Bob Harris>And I was particularly frustrated because this was my father's favorite poem. And he recited it to me pretty constantly. And yet, when they asked me about it under pressure, I just completely choked. And so Brillig became my nickname, for some people.
<v Bob Harris>我感到特别沮丧，因为这是我父亲最喜欢的诗。他经常给我背诵。然而，当他们在压力下问我时，我完全卡住了。所以，有些人给我起了个绰号叫“布里利格”。

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:02.770
<v Ira Glass>I wonder if the reason why you didn't remember it was because it wasn't part of your Jeopardy knowledge, but because it was part of your real knowledge.
<v Ira Glass>我想知道你没记住的原因，是不是因为它不是你《危险边缘》知识储备的一部分，而是你真实知识的一部分。

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:15.760
<v Bob Harris>I think that's exactly right. I think there are a lot of times in the game-- most of the big mistakes I ever made were like that, where it wasn't in my Jeopardy notebooks, my study materials, the almanacs.
<v Bob Harris>我想那正是原因所在。我觉得游戏里有很多时候——我犯过的大多数重大错误都是这样的，那些内容并不在我的《危险边缘》笔记本、学习资料或年鉴里。

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.370
<v Ira Glass>It's funny. It's sort of like it was in the wrong section of your brain.
<v Ira Glass>真有趣。就像它被存放在了大脑里错误的区域一样。

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.980
<v Bob Harris>Yeah, exactly. It was in my real brain, the one I walk around with that doesn't have much in it.
<v Bob Harris>是的，完全正确。它在我的“真实大脑”里，就是我平时带着走的、里面没装多少东西的那个。

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:45.560
<v Ira Glass>Talking to Bob about all this, you realize that a show like Jeopardy, a quiz show, any quiz show on the surface seems like it's about facts, retrieving facts to win prizes. But what's really going on for the players is totally different than just retrieving facts. There's a whole inner world happening, an inner world that is not on TV at all, an inner world that actually may be a lot more interesting than what's in the program that's on TV.
<v Ira Glass>和鲍勃谈论这一切时，你会意识到像《危险边缘》这样的智力竞赛节目，表面上似乎是关于事实的，是为了赢得奖品而提取事实。但对于参赛者来说，真实发生的事情与单纯提取事实完全不同。这是一个完整的内心世界，一个电视上根本看不到的内心世界，一个可能比电视节目本身更有趣的内心世界。

00:03:45.560 --> 00:04:12.440
<v Ira Glass>Well today, we dive in to look at that inner world, at the secret life of quiz shows. From WBEZ Chicago, it's This American Life , distributed by Public Radio International. I'm Ira Glass. Our program today in three rounds. Round One, Gamester of Ireland is Fine. The round is about somebody who goes on to Who Wants to Be a Millionaire , and the most amazing thing he comes up with is not any fact, not any answer, it is the sheer courage to appear at all.
<v Ira Glass>今天，我们将深入探讨那个内心世界，探讨智力竞赛节目的秘密生活。这里是来自芝加哥WBEZ的《美国生活》，由国际公共广播电台发行。我是艾拉·格拉斯。我们今天的节目分为三轮。第一轮，爱尔兰玩家很棒。这一轮讲的是一个参加《谁想成为百万富翁》的人，他带来的最惊人的东西不是任何事实，也不是任何答案，而是他敢于登台的纯粹勇气。

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:23.220
<v Ira Glass>Round Two, Dire Enigmas for Elite Fans, where we visit with some of the best quiz masters anywhere on an all-weekend, all-day, all-night quiz bender.
<v Ira Glass>第二轮，精英粉丝的难题，我们将跟随一些最顶尖的测验大师，进行一场持续整个周末、全天候的测验狂欢。

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:47.730
<v Ira Glass>Round Three, Girls in Need of a Safer Time. By the way, if you are noticing anything special about these round names, five points for you as you play along at home. Anyway, round three is an attempt to use quiz shows-- yes, quiz shows-- to change teenage girls. Stay with us.
<v Ira Glass>第三轮，需要更安全时代的女孩们。顺便提一下，如果你注意到了这些轮次名称有什么特别之处，在家玩的朋友可以给自己加五分。总之，第三轮是试图利用智力竞赛节目——没错，就是智力竞赛——来改变少女。请继续收听。

00:04:47.730 --> 00:05:11.900
<v Ira Glass>Act One, Gamester of Ireland is Fine. When Ronan Kelly went to talk to the guy in this next story, all he knew about him was that he had won a lot of money on a quiz show on RTE, which is the main television station in Ireland. And Ronan just figured that anybody who had won that kind of money must have some kind of story to tell. And anyway, the guy lived nearby. So Ronan got onto his bike with his recording gear, and he bicycled over to the guy's house.
<v Ira Glass>第一幕，爱尔兰玩家很棒。当罗南·凯利去采访这个故事里的主角时，他只知道这人在爱尔兰的主要电视台RTE的一个智力竞赛节目中赢了很多钱。罗南心想，能赢那么多钱的人一定有什么故事可以讲。反正这人就住在附近。于是罗南带着录音设备骑上自行车，骑到了那人的家里。

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:29.300
<v Ira Glass>When he got there, he figured that the first thing they would do is watch the video of the guy on the quiz show. But although this man had won hundreds of thousands of pounds, he actually did not have the technology to do that. What you're about to hear is the story that Ronan put together for Irish radio about this guy. The guy is named Roger Dowds.
<v Ira Glass>他到那里时，心想他们第一件事肯定会看那个人在节目里的录像。但尽管这人赢了数十万英镑，他却根本没有播放设备。你接下来要听的是罗南为爱尔兰电台制作的关于这个人的故事。这个人叫罗杰·多兹。

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:37.280
<v Ronan Kelly>When I got to Roger's house to watch the tape of his appearance, he didn't have a VCR. We had to go back to the radio station to watch it.
<v Ronan Kelly>当我到罗杰家看他参加节目的录像时，他没有录像机。我们不得不回到广播电台去看。

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:40.010
<v Gay Byrne>Roger Dowds from Dublin.
<v Gay Byrne>来自都柏林的罗杰·多兹。

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:42.280
<v Ronan Kelly>January 2001.
<v Ronan Kelly>2001年1月。

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.990
<v Ronan Kelly>Were you told to wave?
<v Ronan Kelly>有人让你挥手吗？

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:48.220
<v Roger Dowds>Oh, yes. They made a big issue about waving and smiling and looking as happy as possible.
<v Roger Dowds>哦，是的。他们特别强调要挥手、微笑，并尽可能看起来快乐。

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.410
<v Gay Byrne>[UNINTELLIGIBLE] from Dublin.
<v Gay Byrne>[听不清]来自都柏林。

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:53.840
<v Gay Byrne>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Gay Byrne>[游戏节目音乐]

00:05:53.840 --> 00:06:03.690
<v Gay Byrne>And it's Fastest Finger first. Stand by your keypads, please.
<v Gay Byrne>现在是“最快手指”环节。请准备好你们的键盘。

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:16.870
<v Ronan Kelly>He was a contestant on the quiz show, Who Wants to Be a Millionaire . I should have put the word "unlikely" in there. Roger was an unlikely contestant, and you'll find out why as the program unfolds.
<v Ronan Kelly>他是智力竞赛节目《谁想成为百万富翁》的参赛者。我本该加上“不可思议的”这个词。罗杰是一位不可思议的参赛者，随着节目的进行，你会发现原因。

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:29.360
<v Gay Byrne>Silence in the studio, please. This is your question. Starting with the largest, arrange these Mediterranean islands in order of size, starting with the largest.
<v Gay Byrne>请演播室保持安静。这是你们的问题。从最大开始，按大小排列这些地中海岛屿，从最大的开始。

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.750
<v Gay Byrne>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Gay Byrne>[游戏节目音乐]

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:35.840
<v Gay Byrne>Crete, Cyprus, Sicily, Malta.
<v Gay Byrne>克里特岛、塞浦路斯岛、西西里岛、马耳他岛。

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:52.150
<v Roger Dowds>Well, there was a phone number you could ring on RTE, obviously. And I rang many times, anyway, with no luck. And eventually, I got a call from someone to say I'd been short-listed. It was a couple of days before the show. You know, they said, oh, you're allowed to have five Phone-a-Friends.
<v Roger Dowds>嗯，RTE有个电话号码可以打，显而易见。反正我打了很多次，没中。最后，有人打电话给我说我进入了入围名单。那是在节目开始前几天。你知道，他们说，噢，你可以有五个场外求助人。

00:06:52.150 --> 00:07:04.020
<v Roger Dowds>I don't have many close friends, so I got two of my brothers. I got someone I play table tennis with. I got the husband of someone I play badminton with, a friend of my brother's, I think. They were the five.
<v Roger Dowds>我没什么亲密朋友，所以找了两个兄弟。找了一个跟我一起打乒乓球的人。找了跟我一起打羽毛球的人的丈夫，还有一个是我兄弟的朋友，我想。就是这五个。

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:14.130
<v Gay Byrne>And who got there quickest? Two right answers. But Roger Dowds beat it at 4.9 seconds. 4.9 seconds. Well done, Roger. There you go.
<v Gay Byrne>谁最快？两个正确答案。但罗杰·多兹以4.9秒的速度胜出。4.9秒。干得好，罗杰。给你。

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:29.700
<v Roger Dowds>You know, I wasn't one of these so-called professional quiz people. I'm not an outgoing enough person to be like that, really. People were astounded that I would think of going on Who Wants to Be a Millionaire .
<v Roger Dowds>你知道，我不是那种所谓的职业测验选手。我这人不够外向，真的。人们对我想去参加《谁想成为百万富翁》感到震惊。

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:44.680
<v Gay Byrne>Now ladies and gentlemen, our next contestant is Roger Dowds. He works as a maintenance assistant in a nursing home. And he lives in Glasnevin in Dublin. And he specifically wants me to mention that his mother, Nora, is deceased, but would be very proud, indeed, to see him on this show.
<v Gay Byrne>女士们先生们，下一位参赛者是罗杰·多兹。他在一家疗养院做护理助理。住在都柏林的格拉斯内文。他特别让我提一下，他的母亲诺拉已经去世了，但如果能看到他参加这个节目，她一定会感到非常自豪。

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:45.750
<v Ronan Kelly>Why did you say that?
<v Ronan Kelly>你为什么要说这个？

00:07:45.750 --> 00:08:00.220
<v Roger Dowds>Well, I still was getting over my mother's death somewhat at the time. She was about three years' dead at the time. And she had been such a part of my life. She probably was quite concerned about my future when she died.
<v Roger Dowds>嗯，当时我还在努力从母亲去世的阴影中走出来。她去世大概三年了。她是我生命中如此重要的一部分。她在去世时可能很担心我的未来。

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:08.690
<v Gay Byrne>And if he won GBP 1 million, he says, he'd help the residents of the nursing home where he works to buy a place and run it however they please. And then he would love to have enough money--
<v Gay Byrne>他说，如果赢了100万英镑，他会帮助疗养院的居民买个地方，随心所欲地经营。然后他会希望能有足够的钱——

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:22.620
<v Roger Dowds>You know, because you don't really believe you're going to be on, and you go through a lot of questions, what you might say in a circumstance, and I kind of said something very frivolous, expecting not to ever be saying anything.
<v Roger Dowds>你知道，因为你根本不相信自己会入选，你会在那种情况下想很多问题，可能会说什么，我当时随口说了些非常轻率的话，完全没想到真的会说出口。

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.500
<v Gay Byrne>All right, good luck to you. Let's play Who Wants to Be a Millionaire .
<v Gay Byrne>好的，祝你好运。让我们开始《谁想成为百万富翁》。

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:27.490
<v Gay Byrne>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Gay Byrne>[游戏节目音乐]

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:33.800
<v Gay Byrne>[APPLAUSE]
<v Gay Byrne>[掌声]

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:49.680
<v Gay Byrne>And for GBP 100, answer this one, Roger. In the 1968 cartoon, what was the color of the Beatles' submarine? Was it blue, yellow, green, or red?
<v Gay Byrne>为了100英镑，回答这个问题，罗杰。在1968年的动画片中，甲壳虫乐队的潜水艇是什么颜色的？是蓝色、黄色、绿色还是红色？

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:50.880
<v Roger Dowds>Yellow. OK.
<v Roger Dowds>黄色。好的。

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:56.820
<v Gay Byrne>For GBP 100, yellow is right. You've got GBP 100, Roger.
<v Gay Byrne>为了100英镑，黄色是正确的。你赢了100英镑，罗杰。

00:08:56.820 --> 00:09:00.810
<v Ronan Kelly>Financially, how were things at the time? Was that an interest for you?
<v Ronan Kelly>财务上，当时情况如何？这对你来说是个考虑因素吗？

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:24.930
<v Roger Dowds>Yes, it was a factor. I never had full-time employment ever in my life. I was at the time working in this home. But I was only working part-time. And I might have done the odd little odd job, but I was on an extremely low income. So I suppose the money aspect could be significant to me and my position.
<v Roger Dowds>是的，是个因素。我这辈子从未有过全职工作。我当时在那家养老院工作。但只是兼职。我可能做过一些零工，但我收入极低。所以我想金钱方面对我来说意义重大。

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.350
<v Roger Dowds>It's not the other name. So Bill.
<v Roger Dowds>那不是另一个名字。所以，比尔。

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:27.790
<v Gay Byrne>Bill?
<v Gay Byrne>比尔？

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:28.690
<v Roger Dowds>That's my answer.
<v Roger Dowds>那是我的答案。

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:29.580
<v Gay Byrne>For GBP 500?
<v Gay Byrne>为了500英镑？

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:30.250
<v Roger Dowds>Yeah.
<v Roger Dowds>是的。

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:34.900
<v Gay Byrne>You've got it. It's the Bill. GBP 500.
<v Gay Byrne>你答对了。比尔。500英镑。

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:37.350
<v Ronan Kelly>Did you practice first?
<v Ronan Kelly>你练习过吗？

00:09:37.350 --> 00:10:08.550
<v Roger Dowds>No, there wasn't time to practice. I didn't practice at all. I remember going in the day, and there were all the other contestants. And some of them were poring over quiz books. I just was trying to cope with being there. They made a tremendous day out of it. You were kind of treated like royalty. We were chauffeur-driven in. I think we got a very special lunch that no one else in RTE was getting.
<v Roger Dowds>不，没时间练习。我根本没练。我记得去的那天，其他选手都在。有些人正在埋头苦读智力题库。我只是努力让自己适应待在那儿。他们把那天办得很隆重。我们像皇室成员一样受到款待。我们是坐专车进去的。我想我们吃了RTE其他人没吃到的特别午餐。

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:25.890
<v Roger Dowds>And I remember thinking, oh, something different is happening today, because I saw some of the people that I recognize who were actors in Fair City. And, I don't know, one or two-- someone who's in Sport in RTE, in addition to all these people. And I don't know whether I'm starstruck or not.
<v Roger Dowds>我记得当时想，噢，今天发生了不寻常的事，因为我看到了一些我认出来的演员，他们演过《Fair City》。还有，不知道，一两个——有人是RTE体育频道的，除了所有这些人。我不知道自己是不是被明星光环震住了。

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:29.000
<v Gay Byrne>No doubt about that one. You have GBP 1,000. [UNINTELLIGIBLE] is the right answer.
<v Gay Byrne>毫无疑问。你有1000英镑。[听不清]是正确答案。

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:29.480
<v Gay Byrne>[APPLAUSE]
<v Gay Byrne>[掌声]

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:37.300
<v Gay Byrne>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Gay Byrne>[游戏节目音乐]

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:44.950
<v Gay Byrne>Now, you can never sit in the chair where Roger is sitting if you don't take those telephone numbers. They're 1550-717171 [UNINTELLIGIBLE].
<v Gay Byrne>现在，如果你不拨打那些电话号码，你就永远无法坐在罗杰坐的那把椅子上。号码是1550-717171[听不清]。

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:48.930
<v Roger Dowds>I'll remember that phone number for the rest of my life.
<v Roger Dowds>我会终生记住那个电话号码。

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:52.440
<v Gay Byrne>Do you want to tell the audience what happened to you in Morocco, Roger?
<v Gay Byrne>你想告诉观众你在摩洛哥发生了什么吗，罗杰？

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:53.310
<v Roger Dowds>Well, I--
<v Roger Dowds>嗯，我——

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.580
<v Roger Dowds>Well, no I don't. You're going to make me, anyway.
<v Roger Dowds>好吧，我不想。反正你都要让我说。

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:58.200
<v Roger Dowds>I was there last month, in fact, in December--
<v Roger Dowds>事实上，我上个月，也就是十二月，就在那儿——

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.590
<v Roger Dowds>I didn't really want to be distracted by anecdotes.
<v Roger Dowds>我真的不想被轶事分散注意力。

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:09.580
<v Roger Dowds>Moroccan dirham, as they call the currency there. So being a bit shy and retiring, I wanted to get rid of them. And all I could find was an Irish--
<v Roger Dowds>摩洛哥迪拉姆，他们那儿叫那种货币。所以因为有点害羞和内向，我想把它们处理掉。我能找到的只有爱尔兰——

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:16.080
<v Ronan Kelly>Where does this sensitivity come from, this lack of confidence come from?
<v Ronan Kelly>这种敏感、这种缺乏自信是从哪儿来的？

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:37.310
<v Roger Dowds>I'm still trying to work that one out. Well, I was uncommonly close my mother. And I was reluctant to go out into the world and do things as a result. I was almost reclusive in kind of a way, because I didn't go out. I did go to college for a while, and it didn't work out.
<v Roger Dowds>我还在努力弄清楚这个问题。嗯，我和我母亲异常亲近。结果我不太愿意进入社会去做事。我几乎是以一种隐居的方式生活，因为我不出去。我有过一段时间去上大学，但没成功。

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:38.810
<v Ronan Kelly>This is in your early 20s?
<v Ronan Kelly>这是你20岁出头的时候？

00:11:38.810 --> 00:11:42.050
<v Roger Dowds>Yeah, I was about 21 at the time.
<v Roger Dowds>是的，当时我大约21岁。

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:44.730
<v Gay Byrne>GAA fan, are you?
<v Gay Byrne>你是盖尔运动协会（GAA）的粉丝吗？

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:52.020
<v Roger Dowds>Actually not particularly, but I had that answer before the counties came up. So I think I--
<v Roger Dowds>事实上并没有特别喜欢，但在郡名出来之前我就知道答案了。所以我认为我——

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:52.240
<v Gay Byrne>You're going with that?
<v Gay Byrne>你决定选那个？

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:54.200
<v Roger Dowds>--have to go with that.
<v Roger Dowds>——必须选那个。

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.990
<v Gay Byrne>Final answer, Kildare?
<v Gay Byrne>最终答案，基尔代尔？

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:58.730
<v Roger Dowds>Final answer.
<v Roger Dowds>最终答案。

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.420
<v Gay Byrne>And it makes you worth GBP 8,000, Roger.
<v Gay Byrne>这让你赢得了8000英镑，罗杰。

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.730
<v Gay Byrne>[APPLAUSE]
<v Gay Byrne>[掌声]

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:05.590
<v Gay Byrne>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Gay Byrne>[游戏节目音乐]

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:50.560
<v Roger Dowds>My father, I suppose, was a little distant from us. It was hard to get any sense of what he expected from us. I sort of feel, in some ways, he was a bit childlike, so sometimes I felt I was fighting for my mother's affection with him. And we had this kind of slightly niggly, sort of relationship as a result. I suppose we were all a bit on our own little wavelength. I was so much younger than the rest, so I think that separated me a bit.
<v Roger Dowds>我想我父亲和我们之间有点疏离。很难知道他从我们身上期待什么。我觉得在某些方面，他有点像孩子，所以有时我觉得自己在和他争夺母亲的爱。结果我们之间有一种略带摩擦的关系。我想我们都有点在各自的频道上。我比其他人小得多，所以我觉得那让我有点疏远。

00:12:50.560 --> 00:13:05.250
<v Roger Dowds>I feel as it's a historical question, now I have a brother who's-- he is a bit of a historian. He studied history. So I think maybe I should phone him. It's my brother, Robert.
<v Roger Dowds>我觉得这是一个历史问题，现在我有位兄弟——他算个历史爱好者。他学过历史。所以我想也许我该打电话给他。是我兄弟，罗伯特。

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:07.820
<v Gay Byrne>Your brother Robert. OK. Robert.
<v Gay Byrne>你兄弟罗伯特。好的。罗伯特。

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:10.270
<v Gay Byrne>[PHONE RINGING]
<v Gay Byrne>[电话铃响]

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:11.190
<v Robert Dowds>Hello.
<v Robert Dowds>你好。

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.460
<v Gay Byrne>Hello, Robert.
<v Gay Byrne>你好，罗伯特。

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:13.370
<v Robert Dowds>Yes, hello.
<v Robert Dowds>是的，你好。

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:16.680
<v Gay Byrne>Good evening to you. This is Gay Byrne on Who Wants to Be a Millionaire.
<v Gay Byrne>晚上好。我是《谁想成为百万富翁》的盖·伯恩。

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:17.650
<v Robert Dowds>Hello.
<v Robert Dowds>你好。

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:23.570
<v Gay Byrne>And your brother Roger has made it to the hot seat. And he needs your help in answering a question, all right?
<v Gay Byrne>你兄弟罗杰已经进入了热座。他需要你的帮助来回答一个问题，好吗？

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:24.310
<v Robert Dowds>Thanks very much.
<v Robert Dowds>非常感谢。

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:32.960
<v Gay Byrne>There are four possible answers to this question. The next voice you hear will be his. And Roger, you have 30 seconds, starting now.
<v Gay Byrne>这个问题有四个可能的答案。你接下来听到的声音就是他的。罗杰，你有30秒时间，现在开始。

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:46.250
<v Roger Dowds>Robert, where did the Asgard land guns for the Irish Volunteers in July 1914? Was it Banna Strand, Scarriff, Howth, or Arklow?
<v Roger Dowds>罗伯特，1914年7月，阿斯加德号在何处为爱尔兰志愿军运送了武器？是班纳海滩、斯卡里夫、霍斯，还是阿克洛？

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:47.770
<v Robert Dowds>Howth.
<v Robert Dowds>霍斯。

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:50.580
<v Roger Dowds>Thank you very much. You're sure about that?
<v Roger Dowds>非常感谢。你确定吗？

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.570
<v Robert Dowds>About 95%.
<v Robert Dowds>95%左右。

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:55.070
<v Roger Dowds>I thought it might be that myself. So thank you.
<v Roger Dowds>我自己也想可能是那个。所以谢谢你。

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:55.960
<v Robert Dowds>OK. Bye.
<v Robert Dowds>好的。再见。

00:13:55.960 --> 00:14:03.130
<v Roger Dowds>Thank you very much. Bye. I'll go with that. Howth.
<v Roger Dowds>非常感谢。再见。我就选那个了。霍斯。

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:04.240
<v Gay Byrne>Howth, final answer?
<v Gay Byrne>霍斯，最终答案？

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:08.460
<v Roger Dowds>Final answer.
<v Roger Dowds>最终答案。

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:16.050
<v Gay Byrne>Could Roger be right in saying Howth for the answer? We'll take a break here. Come back to us after this. Thank you.
<v Gay Byrne>罗杰说霍斯是对的吗？我们休息一下。广告后见。谢谢。

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:16.480
<v Gay Byrne>[APPLAUSE]
<v Gay Byrne>[掌声]

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.340
<v Gay Byrne>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Gay Byrne>[游戏节目音乐]

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:22.700
<v Ronan Kelly>Can you remember the day you decided that college wasn't for you or that college wasn't working out?
<v Ronan Kelly>你还记得那天你决定大学不适合你，或者大学进展不顺利的时候吗？

00:14:22.700 --> 00:15:09.240
<v Roger Dowds>Oh, I didn't feel part of anything there. And I had all sorts of essays and assignments that I was supposed to have done. And I hadn't started on anything. And just one day, I didn't go in. I was so lacking in resources to deal with things then that I couldn't tell anyone. I actually pretended for a whole term to go to college. I spent most of the days like a homeless person, walking around town. Whatever I did. I brought in my sandwiches just as I normally had done. And my brother, in particular, was trying to get me to go back. But it just didn't seem possible. It was simple as that.
<v Roger Dowds>噢，我觉得我在那儿不属于任何群体。我本该完成的所有论文和作业，我一项都没开始。有一天，我就没去学校。当时我缺乏处理问题的资源，以至于我没法告诉任何人。我甚至假装上了一个学期的大学。我大部分时间都像个无家可归的人，在城里晃荡。无论我做什么。我像往常一样带上三明治。我的兄弟特别试图让我回去。但这似乎根本不可能。就这么简单。

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:20.250
<v Gay Byrne>The question was, where did the Asgard land guns for the Irish Volunteers in July 1914? He had to check with his brother, Robert. Robert said Howth. He went with Howth. That was his final answer. And it means he's worth GBP 16,000.
<v Gay Byrne>问题是，1914年7月阿斯加德号在何处为爱尔兰志愿军运送武器？他不得不咨询他的兄弟罗伯特。罗伯特说是霍斯。他选了霍斯。那是他的最终答案。这意味着他赢得了16000英镑。

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:23.620
<v Gay Byrne>[APPLAUSE]
<v Gay Byrne>[掌声]

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:27.480
<v Gay Byrne>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Gay Byrne>[游戏节目音乐]

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:37.330
<v Gay Byrne>The next question is worth GBP 32,000, Roger. OK. Have a look at it. Who was the first person to run a mile in under four minutes?
<v Gay Byrne>下一个问题价值32000英镑，罗杰。好的。看一眼。谁是第一个在四分钟内跑完一英里的人？

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.610
<v Roger Dowds>I couldn't believe my luck with this question.
<v Roger Dowds>我简直不敢相信我的运气能遇到这个问题。

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:43.480
<v Gay Byrne>Sebastian Coe, Harold Abrahams--
<v Gay Byrne>塞巴斯蒂安·科，哈罗德·亚伯拉罕——

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:44.230
<v Ronan Kelly>You're shaking your head.
<v Ronan Kelly>你在摇头。

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:47.470
<v Roger Dowds>Yeah, because I'm going to know it before I see any answers.
<v Roger Dowds>是的，因为在看到答案之前我就知道它了。

00:15:47.470 --> 00:16:02.230
<v Roger Dowds>Well, I think you arranged this question for me, because it just happens it's my namesake, Roger Bannister. I've always had an interest in athletics. And I'm quite sure about this one. Roger Bannister. 1954, I believe it was.
<v Roger Dowds>嗯，我想你一定是为我安排了这个题目，因为碰巧那是我的同名者，罗杰·班尼斯特。我一直对田径运动很感兴趣。而且我很确定这个答案。罗杰·班尼斯特。我相信是1954年。

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:06.940
<v Roger Dowds>[LAUGHTER]
<v Roger Dowds>[笑声]

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.960
<v Gay Byrne>Roger, don't confuse me with dates.
<v Gay Byrne>罗杰，别用日期来困扰我。

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.260
<v Roger Dowds>I'm sorry.
<v Roger Dowds>对不起。

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:15.910
<v Roger Dowds>I felt I should be offering more information.
<v Roger Dowds>我觉得我本应该提供更多信息。

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:24.710
<v Gay Byrne>Whatever about the angels, Roger. I think mama's looking after you as well, is she? Because you've just won GBP 32,000.
<v Gay Byrne>不管天使的事了，罗杰。我想妈妈也在保佑你吧？因为你刚刚赢了32000英镑。

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:25.620
<v Gay Byrne>[APPLAUSE]
<v Gay Byrne>[掌声]

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:29.250
<v Gay Byrne>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Gay Byrne>[游戏节目音乐]

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:34.870
<v Roger Dowds>The crowd seemed to get particularly enthusiastic at that point.
<v Roger Dowds>在那一刻，观众们似乎特别热情。

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:37.010
<v Ronan Kelly>They must have all those checks written out, do they?
<v Ronan Kelly>他们一定准备好支票了吧？

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:41.490
<v Roger Dowds>Oh, yes. Yeah, yeah. There's no writing involved.
<v Roger Dowds>噢，是的。是的，不需要亲笔写。

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:46.460
<v Gay Byrne>GBP 32,000. And you get to keep that. Nobody can take that from you.
<v Gay Byrne>32000英镑。你可以保留。没人能从你这儿拿走。

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:46.920
<v Roger Dowds>No matter what.
<v Roger Dowds>无论如何。

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:53.790
<v Gay Byrne>No matter what, that's yours, OK? And you're right. Bannister did run the mile in 1954, not that we asked you.
<v Gay Byrne>无论如何，那都是你的，明白吗？而且你是对的。班尼斯特确实在1954年跑完了一英里，虽然我们没问你日期。

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:57.210
<v Ronan Kelly>Did your mother encourage you to go out into the world?
<v Ronan Kelly>你母亲鼓励你进入社会吗？

00:16:57.210 --> 00:17:14.550
<v Roger Dowds>She did try to encourage me when I left college. She was always looking at courses that I might do. Because I used to do the garden at home or I did a bit of cooking at home, oh, will you do a cookery course? Will you do a gardening course? You know, just to see me doing something.
<v Roger Dowds>我离开大学时她确实鼓励过我。她总是寻找我可能会参加的课程。因为我以前在家里打理花园或做点饭，噢，你要不要参加烹饪课程？要不要参加园艺课程？你知道，就是想看我做点什么。

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:29.390
<v Roger Dowds>But then I gradually-- as my parents got older, they started becoming infirm. And I did become more of a benefit, because I just became their chauffeur and stuff like that.
<v Roger Dowds>但后来我逐渐——随着父母变老，他们身体开始虚弱，我确实变得更有用了，因为我成了他们的司机之类的人。

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:31.510
<v Ronan Kelly>Was it a time you felt good about yourself?
<v Ronan Kelly>那是你自我感觉良好的时光吗？

00:17:31.510 --> 00:18:04.400
<v Roger Dowds>I think I felt better that I had some little sense of duty in doing something. Because when I was first at home and my parents were still a bit active, I remember, literally, sometimes that people came in during the day and maybe they thought I should be out. And I'd actually literally hide under the bed-- a grown man in his 20s-- just to avoid having to explain myself.
<v Roger Dowds>我觉得我对自己有点责任感，这让我感觉好些。因为当我刚待在家里、父母还活跃的时候，我记得，真的，有时白天有人进来，他们可能认为我应该出去。我真的会躲在床底下——一个20多岁的成年男人——只是为了避免向人解释自己。

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:11.320
<v Ronan Kelly>That must have made you so angry.
<v Ronan Kelly>那一定让你感到非常愤怒。

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:34.480
<v Roger Dowds>I couldn't express anger. I was such a-- I don't know-- such a-- well, withdrawn from anger. I was angry in some way. But I didn't recognize it as anger. Well, I was so full of self-hatred. I didn't have any sense of self-esteem. So I think because of that I couldn't do things at all.
<v Roger Dowds>我没法表达愤怒。我是如此一个——我不知道——如此一个——嗯，远离愤怒的人。我在某种程度上很愤怒。但我没认出那是愤怒。嗯，我充满了自我厌恶。我没有任何自尊。所以我认为因为那个，我根本做不了事。

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:40.180
<v Roger Dowds>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Roger Dowds>[游戏节目音乐]

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:46.600
<v Roger Dowds>I think I have nothing to lose. I shall go for Venus as my final answer.
<v Roger Dowds>我想我没什么可失去的。我决定选“金星”作为最终答案。

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.300
<v Gay Byrne>That's your final answer?
<v Gay Byrne>那是你的最终答案？

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:49.420
<v Roger Dowds>Final answer.
<v Roger Dowds>最终答案。

00:18:49.420 --> 00:19:01.240
<v Gay Byrne>Venus, final answer. You had GBP 32,000, Roger. You now have GBP 64,000.
<v Gay Byrne>金星，最终答案。你之前有32000英镑，罗杰。你现在有64000英镑。

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:06.720
<v Gay Byrne>[APPLAUSE]
<v Gay Byrne>[掌声]

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:16.180
<v Gay Byrne>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Gay Byrne>[游戏节目音乐]

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:19.160
<v Roger Dowds>The biscuits are from the [UNINTELLIGIBLE] cookery book.
<v Roger Dowds>这些饼干是来自[听不清]烹饪书。

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:34.040
<v Ronan Kelly>Tea and biscuits in Roger's house. The biscuits are on a plate bought by his family to support the Protestant side in the 1957 boycott, where Catholics boycotted Protestant businesses, and Protestants, like Rogers' family, bought things to keep those businesses alive.
<v Ronan Kelly>罗杰家里的茶和饼干。饼干放在一个盘子里，那是他的家人在1957年抵制运动期间为了支持新教徒一侧而买的，当时天主教徒抵制新教徒的生意，而像罗杰家这样的新教徒则通过购买来维持这些生意。

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:39.910
<v Roger Dowds>She compiled a cookery book, which seemed to go all around Protestant communities around Ireland.
<v Roger Dowds>她编写了一本烹饪书，似乎在爱尔兰各地的新教社区流传。

00:19:39.910 --> 00:20:07.700
<v Ronan Kelly>Roger felt isolated as a child. And the fact that he was part of a minority community only made that feeling of isolation more intense. But being a Protestant also got him out of the house. He travels miles to play racket sports in clubs that used to be exclusive to his church, something that's no longer the case, and he's glad of that. He goes out to play the organ at church services. And through the church community, he found work in a retirement home set up originally for Protestant residents.
<v Ronan Kelly>罗杰小时候感到孤独。而他是少数群体社区的一员，使这种孤独感更加强烈。但作为新教徒也让他有机会走出家门。他长途跋涉到以前曾是他教会专属的俱乐部去参加球拍运动，现在情况不再是那样了，他对此感到高兴。他出去在教堂礼拜中弹奏管风琴。通过教会社区，他在一家最初为新教居民建立的养老院找到了工作。

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:48.810
<v Roger Dowds>I mean, it has been a tremendous experience over the years. I met some very special people who have passed away because they were old. Well, my mother died at the end of 1997. And shortly after that a woman called Joyce [? Schultheis ?] came into the home. And she just was a tremendous-- excuse me crying-- but gift to me at the time.
<v Roger Dowds>我的意思是，这些年来这是一次极其美妙的经历。我遇到了一些非常特别的人，他们因为年老而去世了。嗯，我母亲在1997年底去世了。在那之后不久，一个叫乔伊斯[听不清]的女人进了养老院。她对我当时来说简直是一个——对不起我哭了——但确实是一个礼物。

00:20:48.810 --> 00:21:16.000
<v Roger Dowds>From the generation she came from, she was a person of rare understanding. You could tell her anything, and she was unshockable. And because of the slightly narrow environment I'd been living in, I felt things had to be kept secret and kind of hidden. Suddenly, I got this different perspective.
<v Roger Dowds>从她那一辈人来看，她是一个极其通情达理的人。你可以告诉她任何事，她都镇定自若。由于我生活在稍微狭窄的环境中，我觉得事情必须保密和隐藏。突然间，我得到了一个不同的视角。

