<v Gay Byrne>[掌声]

00:22:22.930 --> 00:22:39.420
<v Roger Dowds>Around the time I was on Who Wants to Be a Millionare, I started going to a counselor, who I'm still going to. I think she's helped with sort of relieving me after the awful self-hatred.
<v Roger Dowds>在我参加《谁想成为百万富翁》的时候，我开始去看心理医生，我现在还在看。我想她帮助我缓解了可怕的自我厌恶。

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:42.310
<v Ronan Kelly>Why did you decide you needed her?
<v Ronan Kelly>你为什么决定你需要她？

00:22:42.310 --> 00:23:15.880
<v Roger Dowds>I got very friendly with quite an elderly man. And as I said, it was the summer just before I went to school. Oh, sorry, college. And I used to go and visit him. And unfortunately, he started abusing me. And although I was 18, I suppose I was 12. I hadn't had sex education of any kind.
<v Roger Dowds>我和一位相当老的人变得非常亲近。就像我说的，那是我上学校之前的那个夏天。噢，抱歉，大学。我经常去拜访他。不幸的是，他开始虐待我。尽管我18岁了，我猜我只有12岁。我没有接受过任何形式的性教育。

00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:55.790
<v Roger Dowds>I didn't really consent to anything, but I allowed this to happen for about a year, I don't know, because I suppose in some way I valued his attention. And finally-- because I'd never not confided in my mother-- so I did eventually confide in her about this. And it was a very difficult thing for her. She was used to kind of sweeping things aside, putting them under the carpet. I lost a little bit of something with my mother that day.
<v Roger Dowds>我并没有真的同意任何事，但我让这件事发生了一年，我不知道，因为我猜在某种程度上我重视他的关注。最后——因为我从未没对我母亲吐露过——所以我最终还是向她吐露了这件事。这对她来说是一件非常困难的事。她习惯于把事情扫到一边，藏在地毯下。那天我和我母亲之间丢失了一点东西。

00:23:55.790 --> 00:23:57.280
<v Ronan Kelly>I'm sorry. I missed that. You what?
<v Ronan Kelly>抱歉。我没听清。你什么？

00:23:57.280 --> 00:24:07.460
<v Roger Dowds>I kind of lost a little bit of something with my mother. I idealized her so much. And she was so wonderful.
<v Roger Dowds>我和我母亲之间丢失了一点东西。我太理想化她了。她是那么好。

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:10.150
<v Ronan Kelly>And did you go back to the elderly man?
<v Ronan Kelly>你回到那个老人家了吗？

00:24:10.150 --> 00:24:38.760
<v Roger Dowds>I went once. But I didn't-- I remember going once to the door and talking to him. And I made up some outlandish story and, well, lies. So as a result of that, he kind of didn't want to have anything more to do with me anyway. I suppose I pretended I'd gone off with someone else.
<v Roger Dowds>我回去过一次。但我没有——我记得我回去过一次到门口和他交谈。我编造了一些离奇的故事，嗯，谎言。结果，他反正也不想再和我有什么牵扯了。我想我假装我已经和别人走了。

00:24:38.760 --> 00:24:42.490
<v Ronan Kelly>Did he think there was something else in what you were doing?
<v Ronan Kelly>他认为你所做的有别的内容吗？

00:24:42.490 --> 00:24:43.490
<v Roger Dowds>How do you mean? Sorry.
<v Roger Dowds>你是什么意思？抱歉。

00:24:43.490 --> 00:24:50.360
<v Ronan Kelly>Well, did he see it in the same way as you did? Or did he see it as something else? Did he see it as abuse? Or did he see it as a relationship?
<v Ronan Kelly>嗯，他和你从同样的视角看待它吗？还是他将其视为别的东西？他将其视为虐待吗？还是将其视为一段关系？

00:24:50.360 --> 00:25:34.810
<v Roger Dowds>No, he probably saw it as a relationship or something. I don't think he would have had any sense of the abuse I was feeling. At that point, I think I could have let anyone do anything to me. I had so little self-esteem, I suppose I couldn't-- It's like as if I became mute, and I couldn't shout stop.
<v Roger Dowds>不，他可能将其视为一段关系或其他什么。我不认为他会对所感受到的虐待有任何感觉。在那一刻，我想我可以让任何人对我做任何事。我的自尊心太低了，我想我不能——就好像我变得哑巴了，我无法大喊“停”。

00:25:34.810 --> 00:25:36.140
<v Roger Dowds>[GAME SHOW MUSIC]
<v Roger Dowds>[游戏节目音乐]

00:25:36.140 --> 00:25:38.330
<v Roger Dowds>I'm very sure I know this one, Gay.
<v Roger Dowds>我非常肯定我知道这个，盖。

